      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "p2-1-1",
          "panel": 1,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "坂上町の町内会長、梨田と申します",
          "en": "I'm Nashida, Sakagami neighborhood chairman.",
          "note": "A kairanban (“circular board”) is a clipboard of notices passed hand to hand from house to house by the neighborhood association. Many towns still use it."
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-1-2",
          "panel": 1,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "連合会で、回覧をデジタルに、と決まりまして",
          "en": "The federation decided to take the circulars digital."
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-2-1",
          "panel": 2,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "市に伺ったら、支援は来年度からと……",
          "en": "The city said support starts next fiscal year..."
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-3-1",
          "panel": 3,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "で、地下に回された。たらい回しの終点へようこそ",
          "en": "So they sent you to the basement. Welcome to the end of the runaround."
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-4-1",
          "panel": 4,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "地域のデジタル化……本庁に届く……!",
          "en": "Going digital... the main building will notice...!"
        }
      ]
    },
